<title>UK: Winds force closure of Russia's Novorossiisk port.</title>
<headline>Winds force closure of Russia's Novorossiisk port.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Black Sea oil port of Novorossiisk was closed because of high winds and swell on Monday, shipping sources said.</p>
<p>Berth number one was also closed for two weeks of maintenance as scheduled, they added.</p>
<p>The shipping sources said the port was closed at 2255 GMT on Sunday and was still shut on Monday morning. The port authorities were due to make a decision imminently on whether to reopen.</p>
<p>Berth number one is the only one of Novorossisk's berths that can accommodate large tankers of between 100,000 and 140,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kate Dourian, London newsroom +44 171 542 4088</p>
